{
  "name": "Google Sheets to WhatsApp: send a template to each new row and mark it sent",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Google Sheets to WhatsApp\n\nEvery 5 minutes, each row of your sheet with a phone number and no status gets an approved WhatsApp template. The workflow then writes **sent** and the time into that row, or **failed** and the reason, so every row is sent once and you can see what happened.\n\n### Set it up\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-cosend** in Settings > Community nodes, following n8n's [community node installation guide](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/).\n2. Make a sheet with a header row of **phone** and **name**, one customer per row. The workflow adds the **status**, **sent_at** and **error** columns the first time it writes.\n3. Open **Read the sheet**, connect your Google account and pick your sheet from the list. Open **Write the status** and pick the same Google account; it writes to the sheet you picked.\n4. Open **Send WhatsApp template**, add a **Cosend API** credential with your API key (Cosend dashboard > Settings > Developer > API keys).\n5. Pick your approved template and its language. With a workspace key, also pick the WhatsApp number that sends in **Connection**; a connection key already names one.\n6. Turn the workflow on.\n\nTo send a row again, clear its **status**.\n\nTested on n8n 2.46.6 with n8n-nodes-cosend 2026.11.0 (community node; self-hosted n8n)",
        "height": 600,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "3f1c2b7a-5d1e-4c2a-9a51-0b7e3c1d2a01",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -540,
        -240
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### The phone column\nWrite each number with its country code, for example **+44 7700 900123**. The workflow keeps the digits and adds the **+**, so spaces and dashes are fine.",
        "height": 170,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "3f1c2b7a-5d1e-4c2a-9a51-0b7e3c1d2a02",
      "name": "Phone numbers",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        180,
        200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### The template\nWhatsApp lets a business start a conversation with a template Meta approved. Create one in the Cosend dashboard under **Templates**, with one variable for the first name, for example:\n\n*Hi {{1}}, thanks for signing up. Reply here any time.*\n\n**Components** fills that variable from the **name** column. A template with no variables takes **[]**.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "3f1c2b7a-5d1e-4c2a-9a51-0b7e3c1d2a03",
      "name": "Template",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        520,
        200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### The status column\nA row with any status is skipped, so each customer gets the message once.\n\n- **sent**: the message went out at the time in **sent_at**.\n- **failed**: Cosend's reason is in **error**. Fix the row, clear its status, and the next run sends it.\n\nEach run sends to at most 50 rows; the rest go in the next run.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 360,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "3f1c2b7a-5d1e-4c2a-9a51-0b7e3c1d2a06",
      "name": "Status column",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1460,
        240
      ]
    },
    {
